===persian===

نوروز را از شب آغاز کرده‌ایم...
خورشید در راه است... و...
دست‌هایم پر از دانه‌های نیلوفر...
فردا...
بلندترین سایهٔ تو را گل خواهم کاشت...
و... با چشمی آفتابی...
در انتظار خواهم ماند...
۱۳۶۹/۱/۱

===machine===

We have begun Nowruz from the night...
The sun is on its way... and...
my hands are full of lotus seeds...
Tomorrow...
I will plant flowers along your longest shadow...
and... with a sunlit eye...
I will wait...
1369/1/1

===lantern===

We have begun Nowruz from the night...
The sun is on its way... and...
my hands are full of morning-glory seeds...
Tomorrow
I will plant flowers along your longest shadow...
and... with a sunlit eye
I will go on waiting...

1369/1/1

===translation===

===footnotes===

بلندترین سایهٔ تو را گل خواهم کاشت — *I will plant flowers along your longest
shadow* — is a line Jafari had written some thirty years earlier, in the poem that stands here as
longest-shadow (page 31), where planting flowers on the beloved's longest shadow is set against
nailing a tyrant's shortest shadow to the ground. Here the same sentence is emptied of the politics
and planted at Nowruz, at the turn of the year, by a man with his hands full of seed.

